    {
      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Investigate source-level parallelism across independent target bodies in `body_force`, plus the independent position-update loop, using at most the target's 4 CPU cores. Preserve each body's serial `j` accumulation order and ensure all force updates finish before positions change. Keep the existing compiler/toolchain unchanged; if the available build does not support the proposed threading, report that rather than changing it. Measure end-to-end time and correctness.\",\"B\":\"Investigate per-interaction arithmetic improvements, starting with whether a single-precision square-root/reciprocal path is faster than the current `sqrt` double-precision path on ARM64. Check every candidate against the correctness oracle because changed rounding can affect results; reject any that fail. Avoid approximate math or altered summation order unless correctness is demonstrated, and do not change compiler settings.\",\"C\":\"Explore a data-layout and memory-access candidate: stage coordinates (and, if useful, velocities) in structure-of-arrays form to make the O(n²) force loop more contiguous and amenable to existing compiler vectorization, then restore the required `Body` binary output layout. Measure conversion overhead as part of the full run and verify correctness, especially if vectorization changes reduction order. Do not use pairwise-symmetry updates that introduce races or different accumulation semantics.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidates produced by A, B, and C. Use the baseline as a fallback and measure each candidate and promising combination on the unchanged harness: combinations may be slower than their parts. Require correctness across the full supplied case set before selecting an integration; preserve binary I/O and the simulation's iteration count and semantics. Compare against the measured baseline mean of 0.662252 seconds on the 4-core ARM64 target, without specializing to test inputs.\",\"analysis\":\"The measured baseline is valid on all 4 cases, with mean time 0.662252 seconds and score 0.5. The simulation performs ten O(n²) all-pairs force passes, making the force kernel the main optimization opportunity. The three research objectives separate low-risk parallelism, arithmetic, and data layout; each requires end-to-end measurement and correctness checks because numerical changes and combined gains are not guaranteed.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"8579ce88ed7033791822bd0364a47cc59639cf256399abff9872848edf518e36\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Investigate source-level parallelism across independent target bodies in `body_force`, plus the independent position-update loop, using at most the target's 4 CPU cores. Preserve each body's serial `j` accumulation order and ensure all force updates finish before positions change. Keep the existing compiler/toolchain unchanged; if the available build does not support the proposed threading, report that rather than changing it. Measure end-to-end time and correctness.\",\"B\":\"Investigate per-interaction arithmetic improvements, starting with whether a single-precision square-root/reciprocal path is faster than the current `sqrt` double-precision path on ARM64. Check every candidate against the correctness oracle because changed rounding can affect results; reject any that fail. Avoid approximate math or altered summation order unless correctness is demonstrated, and do not change compiler settings.\",\"C\":\"Explore a data-layout and memory-access candidate: stage coordinates (and, if useful, velocities) in structure-of-arrays form to make the O(n²) force loop more contiguous and amenable to existing compiler vectorization, then restore the required `Body` binary output layout. Measure conversion overhead as part of the full run and verify correctness, especially if vectorization changes reduction order. Do not use pairwise-symmetry updates that introduce races or different accumulation semantics.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidates produced by A, B, and C. Use the baseline as a fallback and measure each candidate and promising combination on the unchanged harness: combinations may be slower than their parts. Require correctness across the full supplied case set before selecting an integration; preserve binary I/O and the simulation's iteration count and semantics. Compare against the measured baseline mean of 0.662252 seconds on the 4-core ARM64 target, without specializing to test inputs.\",\"analysis\":\"The measured baseline is valid on all 4 cases, with mean time 0.662252 seconds and score 0.5. The simulation performs ten O(n²) all-pairs force passes, making the force kernel the main optimization opportunity. The three research objectives separate low-risk parallelism, arithmetic, and data layout; each requires end-to-end measurement and correctness checks because numerical changes and combined gains are not guaranteed.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"c6544c8848a545768efb2287f1102dc7\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"8579ce88ed7033791822bd0364a47cc59639cf256399abff9872848edf518e36\",\"session_id\":\"bb7a58941e74486ba24267f2f526de8f\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"66da3b1c1afd4b7badc6787809e2310a117bfe62df3e9ba021679d776e9e005f\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":10520,\"output_tokens\":5041,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":4582}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":15561,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
