      "id": 17,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"synthesis\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Explore cache- and layout-aware force-kernel variants, building on the best persistent OpenMP approach. In particular, investigate ways to reuse source coordinates across independent target bodies without changing the ascending source-index accumulation order for any target. The measured six-array SoA conversion was essentially unchanged from baseline (0.66294 s), and the four-target blocked traversal was slower (0.86879 s); do not repeat these unchanged or assume layout changes will help. Preserve the six-float input/output format and judge candidates by end-to-end measurements.\",\"B\":\"Investigate vectorization across independent target bodies while preserving each target's original inner-loop order and floating-point expression. The outer-loop `parallel for simd` candidate measured 0.17146 s, close to the best 0.17026 s persistent-team candidate; `omp simd` without parallelism measured 0.66235 s. Explore only measured, correctness-preserving refinements, such as vectorization within a persistent team. Avoid reductions, reassociation, or approximate math unless correctness for valid inputs is established.\",\"C\":\"Refine the parallel execution policy: one OpenMP team across all ten iterations, static worksharing for force and integration, and a general workload-based serial/parallel cutoff. The fixed 32-body cutoff candidate measured 0.17026 s; the thread-scaled cutoff candidate measured 0.17283 s. Investigate crossover and overhead without tuning to particular test values. Keep the force/integration phase barriers and avoid nested teams or changes to per-body accumulation order.\",\"G\":\"Use the measured persistent-team implementation (0.17026 s versus the 0.66225 s baseline) as a promising integration starting point, not as a guaranteed winner. Integrate tree changes selectively; measure the integrated program end to end and retain a change only if it remains correct and improves measured performance. Re-run the existing correctness checks and timing procedure for the final combination, since gains may not be additive. Preserve the binary format, ten iterations, force equation, and required phase ordering.\",\"analysis\":\"The source performs an all-pairs force calculation for ten iterations. Bodies are independent during the force phase, so parallelizing across target index i is safe when each target keeps its own accumulators and the j loop retains its original order. Integration must follow force computation before the next iteration, so the phase barriers matter. The best measured candidate is about 3.89x faster than baseline; another parallel candidate is close, while the measured layout and blocked-loop experiments did not improve performance. Use those results to prioritize targeted refinements and measure combinations rather than assuming additive gains.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"2947bf51ff986ecf7eb75bc268fc1a1a37ec603025ead5617e3514adcabeede7\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Explore cache- and layout-aware force-kernel variants, building on the best persistent OpenMP approach. In particular, investigate ways to reuse source coordinates across independent target bodies without changing the ascending source-index accumulation order for any target. The measured six-array SoA conversion was essentially unchanged from baseline (0.66294 s), and the four-target blocked traversal was slower (0.86879 s); do not repeat these unchanged or assume layout changes will help. Preserve the six-float input/output format and judge candidates by end-to-end measurements.\",\"B\":\"Investigate vectorization across independent target bodies while preserving each target's original inner-loop order and floating-point expression. The outer-loop `parallel for simd` candidate measured 0.17146 s, close to the best 0.17026 s persistent-team candidate; `omp simd` without parallelism measured 0.66235 s. Explore only measured, correctness-preserving refinements, such as vectorization within a persistent team. Avoid reductions, reassociation, or approximate math unless correctness for valid inputs is established.\",\"C\":\"Refine the parallel execution policy: one OpenMP team across all ten iterations, static worksharing for force and integration, and a general workload-based serial/parallel cutoff. The fixed 32-body cutoff candidate measured 0.17026 s; the thread-scaled cutoff candidate measured 0.17283 s. Investigate crossover and overhead without tuning to particular test values. Keep the force/integration phase barriers and avoid nested teams or changes to per-body accumulation order.\",\"G\":\"Use the measured persistent-team implementation (0.17026 s versus the 0.66225 s baseline) as a promising integration starting point, not as a guaranteed winner. Integrate tree changes selectively; measure the integrated program end to end and retain a change only if it remains correct and improves measured performance. Re-run the existing correctness checks and timing procedure for the final combination, since gains may not be additive. Preserve the binary format, ten iterations, force equation, and required phase ordering.\",\"analysis\":\"The source performs an all-pairs force calculation for ten iterations. Bodies are independent during the force phase, so parallelizing across target index i is safe when each target keeps its own accumulators and the j loop retains its original order. Integration must follow force computation before the next iteration, so the phase barriers matter. The best measured candidate is about 3.89x faster than baseline; another parallel candidate is close, while the measured layout and blocked-loop experiments did not improve performance. Use those results to prioritize targeted refinements and measure combinations rather than assuming additive gains.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"8babfdfb1a104e57b981d31e4c37a81c\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"2947bf51ff986ecf7eb75bc268fc1a1a37ec603025ead5617e3514adcabeede7\",\"session_id\":\"bb7a58941e74486ba24267f2f526de8f\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"6a8fee964309da978da3ef417001deb31150f39ef156a02d34ef00b61da5d877\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":16621,\"output_tokens\":6726,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":6181}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":23347,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
